---
Implement lock-free command queue from GUI to audio thread.

GUI pushes commands (play/stop, BPM change, step toggle, pattern switch, etc.),
audio thread polls and applies. Eliminates all direct GUI->engine writes during playback.

## Design
- Ring buffer of command structs (256 slots, power-of-2)
- Atomic read/write indices (single producer, single consumer)
- Command types: PLAY, STOP, SET_BPM, SET_VOLUME, TOGGLE_STEP, SET_PATTERN, etc.
- GUI writes to ring buffer instead of engine directly
- Audio thread drains queue at start of each process() call

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] No direct engine mutation from GUI thread during playback
- [ ] Command queue ring buffer implemented with atomics
- [ ] All toolbar actions (play/stop/bpm/vol) go through queue
- [ ] Step toggle in drum grid goes through queue
- [ ] Pattern switch goes through queue
- [ ] No audio glitches during rapid GUI interaction

## Test Plan
- [ ] Unit test: queue push/pop with single producer/single consumer
- [ ] Unit test: queue full behavior (drop or block)
- [ ] Integration: toggle play while audio thread is running
- [ ] ASan run: no data races detected under ThreadSanitizer
